#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:17
msgid "Setting Up Your First Godot Tileset!"
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:18
msgid "LET'S GET STARTED!"
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:20
msgid "In this tour, you'll learn how to create and set up a tileset in Godot."
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:23
msgid "You'll create a tileset from scratch, add tiles to it, and use your tileset to draw a simple platform."
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:26
msgid "In the next tour, you'll add collision shapes to your tiles to prevent the player from falling through the platform."
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:44
msgid "TileMapLayer and TileSet"
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:47
msgid "To draw tilemap-based levels, you need two components:"
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:49
msgid "A [b]TileSet[/b]. It's a resource that you assign to a [b]TileMapLayer[/b] node. It defines your available tiles and their properties."
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:50
msgid "A [b]TileMapLayer[/b] node. This node creates a grid where you can draw tiles to create a level."
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:52
msgid "Think of the [b]TileSet[/b] as a palette of stamps to paint with, and the [b]TileMapLayer[/b] node as your canvas."
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:57
msgid "Opening the starting scene"
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:60
msgid "Let's get ready to create the tileset. First, open the starting scene I've prepared: [b]creating_tilesets.tscn[/b]."
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:61
msgid "This scene contains a playable character that can move and jump. We'll use this character to test our tileset once it's created."
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:68
msgid "Creating the TileMapLayer node"
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:71
msgid "Let's create a [b]TileMapLayer[/b] node first. It allows us to easily create and test the [b]TileSet[/b] resource."
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:75
msgid "Create a [b]TileMapLayer[/b] node as a child of the scene root node."
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:87
msgid "Rename the new [b]TileMapLayer[/b] node to [b]Ground[/b]."
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:101
msgid "Creating a TileSet resource"
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:106
msgid "You now have a [b]TileMapLayer[/b] node in your scene. The next step is to create a [b]TileSet[/b] resource that defines the tiles we can use in this layer."
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:107
msgid "In the [b]Inspector[/b] dock, click the field next to the [b]Tile Set[/b] property and select [b]New TileSet[/b]."
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:108
msgid "This creates an empty [b]TileSet[/b] resource that we'll configure in the next steps."
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:112
msgid "Assign a [b]TileSet[/b] resource to the [b]Tile Set[/b] property."
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:129
msgid "Setting the tile size"
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:134
msgid "The engine needs to know the size of individual tiles in the tileset to draw them correctly."
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:135
msgid "The [b]TileSet[/b] resource's [b]Tile Size[/b] property controls the size of each tile in pixels. Its value should match the size of your tile art assets."
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:136
msgid "Our artist drew tiles that are 16x16 pixels. Luckily for us, that's the default value when you create a [b]TileSet[/b] resource! We can use the default value."
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:143
msgid "Opening the TileSet editor"
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:148
msgid "When selecting a [b]TileMapLayer[/b] node, the editor reveals the [b]TileMap editor[/b]. This bottom panel allows you to draw tiles in the level."
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:149
msgid "We don't have any tiles yet, so we cannot draw anything! Open the [b]TileSet editor[/b] so we can start adding tiles to the TileSet."
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:154
#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:398
msgid "Open the TileSet editor."
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:161
msgid "The TileSet editor"
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:166
msgid "The [b]TileSet editor[/b] is where we define our tiles and their properties."
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:167
msgid "The [b]Tile Sources[/b] tab on the left lists textures containing multiple tiles that you add to the tileset."
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:168
msgid "The empty area on the right allows you to select and change the properties of individual tiles in a tile source."
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:174
msgid "Tile sources"
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:179
msgid "We call the texture containing tiles a [b]Tile Source[/b]. It's a single image containing multiple tiles arranged in a grid."
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:180
msgid "To define what tiles are available in the tileset, you add a tile source, and then you define which parts of the images should be usable as tiles."
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:181
msgid "Our artist prepared tile sources for you to use in this module. We'll use this one to create our first tileset:"
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:188
msgid "Understanding tile creation options"
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:193
msgid "There are two ways to create tiles from a source:"
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:195
msgid "[b]Automatically:[/b] Godot creates tiles for all non-transparent regions in the source for you. When you select [b]Yes[/b] in the popup, Godot uses this method."
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:196
msgid "[b]Manually:[/b] You select and create individual tiles yourself."
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:198
msgid "For now we will do this manually (note: A popup will appear in the next step to give you this choice. Remember to select \"No\")."
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:203
msgid "Adding the tile source"
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:208
msgid "Let's add our first tile source. In the [b]FileSystem[/b] dock, locate the image [b]%s[/b]. This image contains all the ground tiles we'll use in our level."
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:209
msgid "Drag and drop it onto the tile source area in the TileSet editor."
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:210
msgid "[b]Important:[/b] Remember to select [b]No[/b] in the popup that'll appear so we can create tiles manually."
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:216
msgid "Add the [b]%s[/b] file to the [b]TileSet[/b] resource."
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:235
msgid "Naming the source"
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:240
msgid "Let's give our source a descriptive name to keep things organized. By default, the name is set to the file name, but we can change it to something simpler."
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:241
msgid "In the middle column of the TileSet editor, set the [b]Name[/b] property to [b]Ground[/b]."
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:246
msgid "Rename the tile source to [b]Ground[/b]."
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:264
msgid "Creating your first tile manually"
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:269
msgid "Now that we have our source, let's create our first tile manually:"
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:271
msgid "Make sure the %s [b]Setup[/b] tool is active in the TileSet editor toolbar"
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:272
msgid "Click on a tile in the source image on the right (choose one of the ground tiles with grass on top)"
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:274
msgid "You'll see a highlighted border around the selected tile, which means it's now available to draw."
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:282
msgid "Create at least one tile by clicking on a tile in the tile source."
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:300
msgid "Opening the TileMap editor"
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:305
msgid "That's it! You've created your first tile."
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:306
msgid "Let's switch to the [b]TileMap[/b] editor to start drawing with our tile."
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:312
#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:436
msgid "Open the TileMap editor."
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:319
msgid "Drawing your first tile"
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:324
msgid "Let's draw with our manually created tile. For that, you need to select the %s [b]Paint Tool[/b] in the TileMap editor toolbar:"
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:325
msgid "1. Make sure the %s [b]Paint Tool[/b] is selected"
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:326
msgid "2. Look at the tile palette on the right side of the editor. You should see your tile there"
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:327
msgid "3. Click on this tile in the palette to select it"
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:338
msgid "Placing the tile"
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:343
msgid "With the %s paint tool and tile selected, you can now place it on the grid."
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:344
msgid "Click in the 2D viewport to draw the tile. Place a tile right below the player character, so they can stand on it."
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:345
msgid "If you're having trouble drawing:"
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:347
msgid "Make sure the %s [b]Select Mode[/b] is active in the viewport toolbar as other modes won't let you draw"
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:348
msgid "Check that your tile is selected in the palette (it should have a highlighted border)"
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:357
msgid "Select Mode"
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:359
msgid "Place a ground tile below the player character."
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:386
msgid "Populating tiles automatically"
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:391
msgid "Instead of enabling tiles in a tile source manually, we can populate them all automatically."
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:392
msgid "Let's return to the [b]TileSet editor[/b] and do that next."
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:405
msgid "Using the auto-creation tool"
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:410
msgid "You can use the auto-creation tool to add all remaining tiles from the tile source at any time:"
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:412
msgid "In the TileSet editor, click the [b]Three Dots[/b] button on the right of the tileset toolbar"
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:413
msgid "Select [b]Create Tiles in Non-Transparent Texture Regions[/b]"
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:415
msgid "All tiles from the tile source will be automatically detected and created!"
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:424
msgid "Returning to the TileMap editor"
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:429
msgid "Now that we have all our tiles available, let's return to the TileMap editor and draw a few more tiles."
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:430
msgid "Click the [b]TileMap button[/b] at the bottom of the editor."
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:443
msgid "Creating platforms"
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:448
msgid "You now have all the tiles needed to create a platform for our character to stand on."
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:449
msgid "In the tile palette on the right, select individual tiles and try to draw a small complete platform in the viewport using the %s [b]Paint Tool[/b]."
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:450
msgid "[b]Left Click[/b] to paint tiles in the viewport and [b]Right Click[/b] to erase them."
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:451
msgid "Take as little or as much time as you'd like to create a platform. This is a moment for you to experiment with the tiles and see how they fit together."
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:462
msgid "Saving the TileSet"
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:467
msgid "Let's save our [b]TileSet[/b] as a resource file so you can reuse it later:"
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:468
msgid "1. In the [b]Inspector[/b], right-click the [b]Tile Set[/b] property"
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:469
msgid "2. Select [b]Save As...[/b] and save it to [b]%s[/b] (Godot will suggest this name by default)"
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:470
msgid "Saving your [b]TileSet[/b] as a separate resource means you can reuse it across multiple [b]TileMapLayer[/b] nodes and game levels without duplicating work."
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:475
msgid "Save the TileSet resource as [b]%s[/b]"
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:484
msgid "Testing the scene"
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:489
msgid "Let's run the scene to test our tilemap with the character. Click the [b]Run Current Scene[/b] button to start the game."
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:490
msgid "You'll notice the character falls right through our tiles. This happens because we haven't added collision shapes to our tileset yet!"
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:491
msgid "The character doesn't \"see\" the tiles as physical objects. We have to add collision shapes to the tiles so the player can stand on them. That's what we'll do in the next tour."
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:499
msgid "Mission accomplished!"
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:500
msgid "CONTINUE"
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:502
msgid "You now know how to create a basic tileset in Godot!"
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:505
msgid "Your progress will be saved if you quit now."
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_your_first_tileset/102_your_first_tileset.gd:508
msgid "In the next tour, we'll add collision shapes to our tiles so the character can stand on them."
msgstr ""
